EXAMPLE a TOOL prints the fields of its ToolSpec and the descriptions of its arguments
  SOURCE TOOL search_scene SCENE RO "Search."
  SOURCE   FLAG tier1
  SOURCE   TIMEOUT 15.0
  SOURCE   MAXCHARS 30000
  SOURCE   ARG query str "Syntax"
  SOURCE   ARG limit int DEFAULT 50
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'search_scene': {
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'category': 'SCENE',
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'effect': 'RO',
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'tier1': True,
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'timeout_s': 15.0,
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'max_chars': 30000,
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec direct_only
  EXPECT rendered.pyparams 'query': "Syntax",
  EXPECT unrendered.pyparams limit

EXAMPLE EXAMPLE on an ARG prints its illustrative value, one without prints nothing
  SOURCE TOOL search_scene SCENE RO "Search."
  SOURCE   ARG query str EXAMPLE "Player"
  SOURCE   ARG limit int DEFAULT 50
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyexamples 'search_scene': {
  EXPECT rendered.pyexamples 'query': "Player",
  EXPECT unrendered.pyexamples limit

EXAMPLE a FORWARD tool prints its expectation and its wrapper, which leaves out an OMIT argument that equals its default
  SOURCE TOOL search_scene SCENE RO "Search."
  SOURCE   FORWARD
  SOURCE   DOC "root: scope \"here\"."
  SOURCE   DOC "limit: max."
  SOURCE   ARG query str
  SOURCE   ARG root ostr DEFAULT None
  SOURCE   ARG limit int DEFAULT 50 OMIT
  SOURCE   ARG count int DEFAULT 5
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect('search_scene', 'RO', "Search.", (
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('root', ostr, None),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('limit', int, 50),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools @tools.provide
  EXPECT rendered.pytools async def search_scene(
  EXPECT rendered.pytools root: ostr = None,
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ("Search."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools "\n    root: scope \"here\"."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools "\n    limit: max."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools query=rt.w_str(query),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools root=rt.w_ostr(root),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools limit=rt.w_int(limit, 50),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools count=rt.w_int(count),

EXAMPLE a BODY tool prints its expectation and a wrapper that calls the hand module instead of _send
  SOURCE TOOL frob SCENE RW "Frob."
  SOURCE   BODY objects
  SOURCE   DOC "a: the thing."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect_body('frob', 'objects')
  EXPECT rendered.pytools @tools.provide
  EXPECT rendered.pytools async def frob(
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ("Frob."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools "\n    a: the thing."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools from .. import objects as _biome_body_mod
  EXPECT rendered.pytools return await _biome_body_mod._frob_body(
  EXPECT rendered.pytools a=a,
  EXPECT unrendered.pytools _send(

EXAMPLE a PYTOOL with BODY prints its expectation, a wrapper that calls the hand module, and its DOC lines
  SOURCE PYTOOL gizmo SYSTEM RW "Gizmo."
  SOURCE   BODY gizmo_tool
  SOURCE   DOC "a: the thing."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect_body('gizmo', 'gizmo_tool')
  EXPECT rendered.pytools @tools.provide
  EXPECT rendered.pytools async def gizmo(
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ("Gizmo."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools "\n    a: the thing."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools from .. import gizmo_tool as _biome_body_mod
  EXPECT rendered.pytools return await _biome_body_mod._gizmo_body(
  EXPECT rendered.pytools a=a,
  EXPECT unrendered.pytools _send(

EXAMPLE a PYTOOL is direct_only, escapes its descriptions, and prints only an expectation like a TOOL that is not FORWARD
  SOURCE PYTOOL use_skill SYSTEM RW "Use."
  SOURCE   ARG name str "say \"hi\" \\ bye"
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RW "X."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'use_skill': {
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'direct_only': True,
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec tier1
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec timeout_s
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec max_chars
  EXPECT rendered.pyparams 'name': "say \"hi\" \\ bye",
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect('use_skill', 'RW', "Use.", (
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect('x', 'RW', "X.", (
  EXPECT unrendered.pytools async def

EXAMPLE the table of the docs has a row per tool: its plane, category and effect
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RW_IDEM "X."
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE PYTOOL y SYSTEM RO "Y."
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.mdtools | `x` | unity | SCENE | RW_IDEM |
  EXPECT rendered.mdtools | `y` | python | SYSTEM | RO |

EXAMPLE a name or an argument twice
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RO "X."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE   ARG a int
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RW "X."
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 3:7
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 5:6

EXAMPLE an effect, a category or a type outside the lists, no summary, OMIT without a default
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE WRITE "X."
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL y SCENES RO "Y."
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL z SCENE RO "Z."
  SOURCE   ARG a integer
  SOURCE   ARG b int OMIT
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL w SCENE RO
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:14
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:9
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:13
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 9:14

EXAMPLE a PYTOOL is direct_only already and has no Unity-side words: unity_transport, MAXCHARS
  SOURCE PYTOOL x SYSTEM RO "X."
  SOURCE   FLAG unity_transport
  SOURCE   FLAG direct_only
  SOURCE   MAXCHARS 5
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD at 4:3

EXAMPLE an argument has a text default, is sent raw, is left out when it equals its default, and may be written in camelCase
  SOURCE TOOL show SCENE RO "Show."
  SOURCE   FORWARD
  SOURCE   ARG mode str DEFAULT_TEXT "all" OMIT
  SOURCE   ARG label str DEFAULT_TEXT "say \"hi\"" "A label"
  SOURCE   ARG depth int DEFAULT 2 RAW
  SOURCE   ARG both int DEFAULT 5 OMIT RAW
  SOURCE   ARG index int RAW
  SOURCE   ARG agentRadius float DEFAULT 0.5
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('mode', str, "all"),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('label', str, "say \"hi\""),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('agentRadius', float, 0.5),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools mode: str = "all",
  EXPECT rendered.pytools depth: int = 2,
  EXPECT rendered.pytools mode=rt.w_str(mode, "all"),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools label=rt.w_str(label),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools depth=rt.w_int(depth, raw=True),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools both=rt.w_int(both, 5, raw=True),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools index=rt.w_int(index, raw=True),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools agentRadius=rt.w_float(agentRadius),
  EXPECT rendered.pyparams 'label': "A label",

EXAMPLE a parameter typed Any and a text default are only expected, for a TOOL and for a PYTOOL
  SOURCE TOOL run_it TESTS RW "Run."
  SOURCE   ARG ctx Any DEFAULT None
  SOURCE   ARG mode str DEFAULT_TEXT "x y" "A mode"
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE PYTOOL py_one SYSTEM RO "Py."
  SOURCE   ARG value Any
  SOURCE   ARG note str DEFAULT_TEXT ""
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('ctx', Any, None),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('mode', str, "x y"),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('value', Any),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('note', str, ""),
  EXPECT rendered.pyparams 'mode': "A mode",
  EXPECT unrendered.pytools async def

EXAMPLE RUNTIME gives runtime_only to a TOOL
  SOURCE TOOL run_it TESTS RW "Run."
  SOURCE   RUNTIME
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'runtime_only': True,

EXAMPLE RUNTIME gives runtime_only to a PYTOOL
  SOURCE PYTOOL py_one SYSTEM RO "Py."
  SOURCE   RUNTIME
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'runtime_only': True,

EXAMPLE a block without RUNTIME is not runtime_only
  SOURCE TOOL calm SCENE RO "Calm."
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE PYTOOL py_one SYSTEM RO "Py."
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec runtime_only

EXAMPLE INTERNAL is a wire command that has a ToolSpec and nothing else
  SOURCE INTERNAL ping RO "Liveness probe."
  SOURCE   TIMEOUT 5.0
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE INTERNAL put_it RW "Import."
  SOURCE   FLAG direct_only
  SOURCE   FLAG unity_transport
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'ping': {
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'category': '_INTERNAL',
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'effect': 'RW',
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'timeout_s': 5.0,
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'unity_transport': True,
  EXPECT unrendered.pytools ping
  EXPECT unrendered.pyparams put_it
  EXPECT unrendered.mdtools ping

EXAMPLE INTERNAL has no effect other than RO and RW, no flag but direct_only and unity_transport, and no RUNTIME
  SOURCE INTERNAL x WRITE "X."
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE INTERNAL y RO "Y."
  SOURCE   FLAG core
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE INTERNAL z RO "Z."
  SOURCE   RUNTIME
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:12
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD at 7:3

EXAMPLE a READ action of a TOOL or a PYTOOL is printed for Python and for C#, a tool without one is not
  SOURCE TOOL scene SCENE RW "Scene."
  SOURCE   ARG action str
  SOURCE   READ list
  SOURCE   READ get_info
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE PYTOOL navmesh_query SCENE RW "NavMesh."
  SOURCE   ARG action str
  SOURCE   READ status
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL calm SCENE RO "Calm."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyreads 'scene': frozenset({
  EXPECT rendered.pyreads 'list',
  EXPECT rendered.pyreads 'get_info',
  EXPECT rendered.pyreads 'navmesh_query': frozenset({
  EXPECT rendered.pyreads 'status',
  EXPECT unrendered.pyreads 'calm'
  EXPECT rendered.csreads case "scene":
  EXPECT rendered.csreads case "list":
  EXPECT rendered.csreads case "get_info":
  EXPECT rendered.csreads case "navmesh_query":
  EXPECT rendered.csreads case "status":
  EXPECT unrendered.csreads case "calm":
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec READ

EXAMPLE a READ action is spelt in lower case, once, and an INTERNAL has none
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RW "X."
  SOURCE   READ Get
  SOURCE   READ list
  SOURCE   READ list
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE INTERNAL y RO "Y."
  SOURCE   READ get
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 4:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD at 7:3

EXAMPLE cstools sorts ARGs into Required/Optional and reads Mutating from effect
  SOURCE TOOL frobnicate SCENE RW "Frob."
  SOURCE   ARG target str
  SOURCE   ARG amount int DEFAULT 5
  SOURCE   ARG label str DEFAULT_TEXT "x"
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "frobnicate":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Mutating = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Required = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "target",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Optional = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "amount",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "label",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),

EXAMPLE cstools prints Mutating false and the empty-array form for a RO TOOL with no ARGs, and omits RUNTIME/MAXCHARS/GUARD/WIRE fields it does not declare
  SOURCE TOOL calm SCENE RO "Calm."
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "calm":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Mutating = false,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Required = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Optional = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools Runtime = true,
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools MaxResponseChars
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools AlwaysAllowed
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools AllowedDuringCompile
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools PlayOk
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools SpecialDispatch
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools NotBatchable
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools NoUndo

EXAMPLE cstools prints RUNTIME, MAXCHARS and every GUARD/WIRE flag when a TOOL declares them
  SOURCE TOOL loaded_up TESTS RW "Loaded."
  SOURCE   RUNTIME
  SOURCE   MAXCHARS 20000
  SOURCE   GUARD always
  SOURCE   GUARD compile
  SOURCE   GUARD play_ok
  SOURCE   WIRE special
  SOURCE   WIRE not_batch
  SOURCE   WIRE no_undo
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "loaded_up":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Runtime = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools MaxResponseChars = 20000,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools AlwaysAllowed = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools AllowedDuringCompile = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools PlayOk = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools SpecialDispatch = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools NotBatchable = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools NoUndo = true,

EXAMPLE cstools prints the empty-array form for an INTERNAL with no ARG and never renders a PYTOOL
  SOURCE INTERNAL stop_it RO "Stop."
  SOURCE   GUARD play_ok
  SOURCE   WIRE no_undo
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE PYTOOL py_side SYSTEM RO "Py."
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "stop_it":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Required = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Optional = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools PlayOk = true,
  EXPECT rendered.cstools NoUndo = true,
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools py_side

EXAMPLE cstools sorts an INTERNAL's ARGs into Required/Optional like a TOOL's
  SOURCE INTERNAL fetch_it RW "Fetch."
  SOURCE   ARG path str
  SOURCE   ARG limit int DEFAULT 10
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "fetch_it":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Required = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "path",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Optional = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "limit",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),

EXAMPLE cstools excludes a LOCAL ARG from both Required and Optional
  SOURCE TOOL frobnicate SCENE RW "Frob."
  SOURCE   ARG target str
  SOURCE   ARG amount int DEFAULT 5
  SOURCE   ARG hidden str LOCAL
  SOURCE   ARG cached int DEFAULT 1 LOCAL
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "frobnicate":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Required = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "target",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Optional = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "amount",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools hidden
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools cached

EXAMPLE cstools emits WIRE's name instead of the ARG's own name in Required/Optional
  SOURCE TOOL relabel SCENE RW "Relabel."
  SOURCE   ARG old_name str WIRE "new_name"
  SOURCE   ARG old_opt str DEFAULT_TEXT "x" WIRE "new_opt"
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.cstools case "relabel":
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Required = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "new_name",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT rendered.cstools Optional = string.Join(",", new string[] {
  EXPECT rendered.cstools "new_opt",
  EXPECT rendered.cstools }),
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools old_name
  EXPECT unrendered.cstools old_opt

EXAMPLE ARG LOCAL and WIRE exclude each other
  SOURCE TOOL conflicted SCENE RW "Conflicted."
  SOURCE   ARG dual str LOCAL WIRE "x"
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic CONSTRUCT_ENSURE at 1:1

EXAMPLE FORWARD and BODY exclude each other
  SOURCE TOOL dual_body SCENE RW "Dual."
  SOURCE   FORWARD
  SOURCE   BODY objects
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic CONSTRUCT_ENSURE at 1:1

EXAMPLE BODY and ARG RAW exclude each other
  SOURCE TOOL dual_body SCENE RW "Dual."
  SOURCE   BODY objects
  SOURCE   ARG a int RAW
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic CONSTRUCT_ENSURE at 1:1

EXAMPLE a tool may declare BODY at most once
  SOURCE TOOL dual_body SCENE RW "Dual."
  SOURCE   BODY objects
  SOURCE   BODY asset
  SOURCE   TAG reflect_silent
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic CONSTRUCT_ENSURE at 1:1

EXAMPLE EXPECT token prints the OR-list and the strict flag, for a TOOL and a PYTOOL
  SOURCE TOOL kick SCENE RW "Kick."
  SOURCE   EXPECT token "Wired|Connected"
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE PYTOOL nudge SYSTEM RW "Nudge."
  SOURCE   EXPECT token "ok" STRICT
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyexpect 'kick': ('token', 'Wired|Connected', False, None),
  EXPECT rendered.pyexpect 'nudge': ('token', 'ok', True, None),

EXAMPLE EXPECT bool_arg prints its ARG and no strict flag
  SOURCE TOOL sweep SCENE RW "Sweep."
  SOURCE   ARG preview bool DEFAULT False
  SOURCE   EXPECT bool_arg "DRY|DELETED" ARG preview
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyexpect 'sweep': ('bool_arg', 'DRY|DELETED', False, 'preview'),

EXAMPLE EXPECT arg_echo prints its arg names as tokens
  SOURCE TOOL tint SCENE RW "Tint."
  SOURCE   ARG hue ostr DEFAULT None
  SOURCE   EXPECT arg_echo "hue"
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyexpect 'tint': ('arg_echo', 'hue', False, None),

